Test Harness
  - The offline test harness under test/ is original Amazon work. It is provided for
    experimental/development use only — to validate transformation logic before deploying to a
    licensed IBM Sterling OMS runtime — and is not a substitute for a licensed IBM Sterling OMS
    environment, which users are expected to obtain for production use. To compile and run the
    production classes locally — without a licensed IBM Sterling OMS runtime and without any
    Amazon connectivity — it provides minimal clean-room re-implementations of the third-party
    API shapes the code imports (IBM Sterling types, the accelerator's own helper classes, and
    Apache HttpComponents placeholders).
  - Only the class/API names and method signatures are reproduced; the implementations are
    entirely original Amazon work, backed by the standard JDK XML / JSON APIs. No IBM
    Sterling-authored code, headers, or libraries are included or redistributed.
  - The test harness depends only on JUnit (EPL-2.0), retrieved from Maven Central at build time,
    and org.json (Apache-2.0) bundled in lib/.
